<title>UK: Ex-dividends take 4.242 points off UK's FTSE index.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends take 4.242 points off UK's FTSE index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE International said the following FTSE 100 stocks go ex-dividend on Monday and the effect will be to take 4.242 points off the index.</p>
<p>					     DIVIDEND	INDEX</p>
<p>					     (PENCE)	 EFFECT</p>
<p>	COMPANY			  Net   Gross    Gross</p>
<p> * Enterprise Oil		   10.50   13.13    0.380</p>
<p> * Prudential Corporation	 11.50   14.38    1.616</p>
<p> * Rank Organisation		12.00   15.00    0.733</p>
<p> * Reckitt &amp; Colman		 14.02   17.52    0.416</p>
<p> * Schroders (ordinary)	   14.00   17.50    0.154</p>
<p> * Schroders (non-voting)	 14.00   17.50    0.046</p>
<p> * TI Group			    9.75   12.19    0.339</p>
<p> * United News &amp; Media	    15.50   19.38    0.557</p>
<p>(a) Net dividend for Reckitt &amp; Colman includes a Foreign Income Dividend (FID) amount of 7.01p gross.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7954</p>
</text>
